Z||000000||DaveL||11-25-2000||09:44 AM||||I know I've asked about this before and gotten some good response, I'm still having a little troublw tih the adjustment of my throttle valve cable. 87 SE 2.5 a/t<BR>Does any one have any pictures of this procedure? The Hayne's Manual leaves a little to be desired....  At the TBI, the cable is attached to a pulley, at the tranny the cable is attached by1 or two small bolts. There's a connection near the trans that comes apart to reveal a metal cable with a little tab. I'm at a loss. I can get a new one from GM for about $35. Maybe smart to get one, then I'll have one to look at. Will the new one be an exact match for the old one???||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-25-2000||03:29 PM||||What cable are you adjusting? <P>do you mean the cable from the TBI idler wheel to the tranny?<P>There's a square button on the side of it. push the button and move the cable jacket in or out of the tranny. <P>Nothing from the button to the tranny moves. The part that moves is the cable jacket above the button. It may be stuck. Make sure you can slide it by hand BEFORE trying the book procedure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaveL||11-25-2000||08:13 PM||||Yes, thats the one. I must be blind! I'm going after it again tomorrow.||||reg||1
